description":"Clemson lost starting QB Tait Reynolds for the rest of the season with a torn meniscus, while backup Christopher Vizzina has a concussion.","published":"2026-11-15T21:09:56.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50493355/reynolds-torn-meniscus-vizzina-concussion","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Minnesota fires OC Greg Harbaugh Jr., ending third stint with Gophers","description":"Minnesota fired offensive coordinator Greg Harbaugh Jr. as the Golden Gophers rank 15th in the Big Ten in scoring and 17th in yards per game.","published":"2026-11-15T19:36:27.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50491908/minnesota-fires-oc-greg-harbaugh-jr-ending-3rd-gophers-stint","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Allstate Playoff Predictor","description":"Select your favorite contender, make your picks for how its season will play out and see what the Allstate Playoff Predictor foretells.","published":"2026-11-15T18:13:44.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/feature/story/_/page/cfbplayoffpredictor/college-football-allstate-playoff-bracket-predictor","type":"Eticket","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 NFL draft questions, latest intel, risers, CFB standouts","description":"Is Jackson Harris the WR3 in the class? And has Boubacar Traore emerged as the No. 3 edge rusher? Here's our weekly draft spin, including top standouts.","published":"2026-11-15T17:34:06.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/49881131/2027-nfl-draft-risers-questions-college-football-prospects","type":"Story","byline":"Mel Kiper Jr. and Jordan Reid","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4819260/adam-trick","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adam_Trick"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Adam Trick","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adam_Trick","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:49Z","intro":"Adam Trick is an American college football linebacker for the Texas Tech Red Raiders. He previously played for the Miami RedHawks.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Trick attended Wayne High School in Huber Heights, Ohio. As a senior he had 65 tackles and two sacks. He committed to Miami University to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"After redshirting his first year at Miami in 2022, Trick played in all 14 games in 2023 and had six tackles. In 2024, he started three of 14 games, recording 37 tackles, 4.5 sacks and an interception. In 2025, Trick was named First-Team All-MAC after finishing with 59 tackles, 8.5 sacks and one interception over 13 starts. After the season, he entered the transfer portal and committed to Texas Tech University."}]}}